;; The reviews of the opam set's golden files (the user's decision of 2026-11-20: reviewed golden files, JCS361 (a)'s way for Java's
;; jtreg tests, test/java/golden/, and c-cpp-golden's for C++'s samples, test/cpp/selfref-golden.edn). The 11 programs below were
;; judged by ocamlc's and ocamlopt's recorded runs alone (test/ocaml/ref-suite.edn): demonstrations their packages do not run as tests
;; (cmdliner's examples and blueprints, ~run:false in its B0.ml; pprint's PPrintTest), with no verdict of their own. Each now has one:
;; test/ocaml/opam/golden/PKG-NAME.reference, its standard output and standard error merged as the harness writes them (bin/oi's
;; run_redirected, `> OUT 2>&1`), byte for byte, and the exit status here, both written from the program's text and the library's
;; source at the pinned version (cmdliner 2.1.1, pprint 20230830: test/ocaml/corpora.edn) with OCaml 5.5.0's stdlib, before they
;; were compared with anything; then checked against the recorded runs' status and SHA-256 (ocamlc's and ocamlopt's, equal for
;; each): 11 of 11 met at the first writing, an agreement found, not used. test/ocaml/opam-verdicts.tsv's `golden` lines name them;
;; bin/oi's own_verdicts takes a golden line as a `file` line (status, SHA-256, bytes) and refuses a golden line without its review
;; here (or whose review gives another status or file) and a review without its golden line: a golden file is a verdict only with
;; its review, and a review only with its golden file. Revolt1's and revolt2's files are the same bytes (two programs, one output).
;; Since queue 528 (the user's decision of 2026-11-22, 528-15) also uutf's utftrip, a corpus row of its own (12 programs).
;; :basis what fixes the output:
;;   :src  the program's own text (the package's test/NAME.ml)
;;   :lib  the library's source (cmdliner's src/: Cmdliner_eval's evaluation, Cmdliner_cline's parse, Cmdliner_docgen's man page,
;;         Cmdliner_manpage's plain renderer, Cmdliner_msg's errors, Cmdliner_base.Fmt's styling; pprint's src/PPrint.ml and
;;         PPrintEngine.ml)
;;   :fmt  OCaml 5.5.0's Format (stdlib/format.ml): std_formatter and err_formatter's margin 78 (pp_make_formatter), a string's
;;         width its UTF-8 scalars (utf_8_scalar_width: "…" counts 1, its 3 bytes written), a break of a box taken when 1 + the
;;         next word would pass column 78 (format_pp_token's Pp_box), the continuation at the box's column; std_formatter flushed
;;         at exit (flush_standard_formatters), err_formatter at each @. of cmdliner's messages
;;   :args the corpus row's arguments (test/ocaml/opam-programs.tsv: --help=plain, or the arguments of an error)
;;   :env  the output's dependence on the environment: cmdliner's styler (Cmdliner_base.Fmt.styler', read at the program's start)
;;         is Ansi when NO_COLOR is unset or empty and TERM is set and not "dumb", else Plain; it shows in an error message only
;;         (the man page in plain format is unstyled: Cmdliner_manpage.doc_to_plain, markup_to_plain ~styled:false). The decision
;;         of 2026-11-20 (judge-rest): example_chorus's and example_rm's corpus rows fix it, TERM=xterm-256color NO_COLOR= (the
;;         ENV column of test/ocaml/opam-programs.tsv, exported by run_redirected for every runner), the styler Ansi as the
;;         recorded runs were made (their 147 and 133 bytes hold the escapes; Plain would print 85 and 87, quoting '-n' and 'a')
;;   :cwd  the run's working directory: no file named a (the staged units and the runner's files only)
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "opam/cmdliner/blueprint_cmds" :status 0 :file "golden/cmdliner-blueprint_cmds.reference" :basis [:src :lib :fmt :args]
  :why "Cmd.group (Cmd.info \"TODO-toolname\" ~version ~doc) [hey_cmd; ho_cmd], no default term; Cmd.eval' with --help=plain.
  Evaluation (cmdliner_eval.ml): find_cmd_and_parser stops at the option, a group without default gives Error (`Parse (try_stdopts =
  true, err_cmd_missing)); add_stdopts adds --help and, the main command having a version, --version; Cmdliner_cline.create parses
  --help=plain (parse_opt_arg: a long option with its glued value) into stdopt_help's (some man_fmts_enum): `Plain; try_eval_stdopts
  gives `Std_help `Plain, do_result prints Cmdliner_docgen.pp_man to Format.std_formatter and returns `Help: exit_status_of_result 0,
  eval' returns it, exit 0. Nothing on stderr (no markup error: every doc string's $(...) is well formed).
  The page (Cmdliner_docgen.text, Cmdliner_manpage.pp_plain_page): the man is empty, so NAME from ensure_s_name, \"TODO-toolname - The
  tool synopsis is TODO\" (invocation, cmd_doc); SYNOPSIS from synopsis: a group without default term (has_args false) is \"$(b,name)
  $(i,COMMAND) …\", plain \"TODO-toolname COMMAND …\"; COMMANDS from cmd_docs: each child's synopsis as label (no options in its
  OPTIONS section: \"[$(i,OPTION)]…\") with its doc, sorted by section then reversed label then rebuilt in order by
  sorted_items_to_blocks: hey, ho; COMMON OPTIONS (the default sdocs) from arg_docs: --help then --version (order_args: the largest
  name, its leading \"--\" read as \"-\": \"-help\" < \"-version\"), the help label synopsis_opt_arg's \"--help[=FMT]\" (Opt_vopt, its
  docv FMT) with \" (default=auto)\" (the vopt Some `Auto printed by the enum), its doc man_fmts_doc \"this help\" with $(docv) FMT and
  man_fmts_alts \"one of auto, pager, groff or plain\" (alts_str, fits in 78); --version is a flag, no absent text, \"Show version
  information.\"; EXIT STATUS from exit_docs: the boilerplate \"$(cmd) exits with:\" (no EXIT STATUS of the program's own) and
  Exit.defaults 0, 123, 124, 125 with their docs; no ENVIRONMENT (no env), no SEE ALSO (the default `Main xref dropped for the main
  command). Section order: Cmdliner_manpage.order, smap_append_block inserting each before the section of the largest lower order.
  Layout (pp_plain_blocks): a section name at column 0; a `P at column 7 (p_indent), then a blank line; an `I's label at 7 and, the
  label 4 bytes or longer (l_indent), its doc on the next line at 11, wrapped at 78 (the help doc: \"...one of auto,\" / \"pager,
  groff or plain. With auto, the format is pager or plain\" / \"whenever the TERM env var is dumb or undefined.\"), a blank line
  after it; the exits' labels shorter than 4 bytes, their doc on the label's line at 11 (\"0   \", \"123 \"). The page ends with
  the last item's line and its blank line: 785 bytes."}
